Software Development Proposal
1. Overview
This proposal outlines the development of a private, intranet-based dashboard for Daikibo. The dashboard will display the health status of the 9 machines located in each of Daikibo’s 4 factories using real-time telemetry data. The solution will integrate with the client’s existing authentication server, ensuring seamless access for authorized personnel. This project aims to provide a reliable and secure overview of machine health to facilitate quick decision-making and maintenance prioritization.
2. Scope
The proposed dashboard will include the following functionality:

- Single-page dashboard: Lists the current status of all monitored devices, with intuitive color-coding and real-time updates.
- Expandable/collapsible view: Users can expand/collapse by factory and device levels to view a historical status log.
- Authentication integration: Syncs with the client’s internal authentication server to allow users to leverage their existing company-wide credentials for secure access.
- Responsive design: Ensures usability across different devices within the intranet environment.
- Error handling: Incorporates mechanisms to handle telemetry errors and display fallback messages where necessary.

